f></ref-list></back><floats-wrap><fig id="fig1"><label>Figure 1</label><caption><p>Cumulative probability of clearance of incident HPV infection, by viral group and age group (under 30 years and 30 years and over), in women with normal cytology at baseline. Number of infections (<italic>n</italic>) with point estimates and 95&#x00025; CI of median duration of infection by age group are reported. HPV16 persisted significantly longer in women under 30 years of age than older women (<italic>P</italic>&#x0003c;0.01, log-rank test).</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" mime-subtype="eps" xlink:href="6604972f1"/></fig><fig id="fig2"><label>Figure 2</label><caption><p>Cumulative probability of clearance of incident HPV infections by viral load (lower and fifth quintile) and viral group, in women with normal cytology at baseline. Viral load was estimated from the optical density and values categorised in quintiles.</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" mime-subtype="eps" xlink:href="6604972f2"/></fig><table-wrap id="tbl1" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p content-type="table-title">Factors associated with clearance of incident infection by HPV types in women with normal cytology at baseline</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="6604972t1"/></table-wrap><table-wrap id="tbl2" position="float"><label>Table 2</label><caption><p content-type="table-title">Risk and HR of high-grade cervical dysplasia (CIN2/3/HSIL) by duration of HPV infection</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="6604972t2"/></table-wrap><table-wrap id="tbl3" position="float"><label>Table 3</label><caption><p content-type="table-title">Risk of high-grade cervical dysplasia (CIN2/3/HSIL) by number of HPV-positive visits</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xlink:href="6604972t3"/></table-wrap></floats-wrap></article>